# MEMORY.md — project-local decisions

> Drop this file at the root of a new project so adk skills load it as repo-local context (per `AGENTS.md` §1.2 — alongside `<repo>/ai-guidelines/` and `<repo>/docs/`). Each entry is one decision with its rejected alternatives so a future-you (or another agent) can avoid re-litigating it.
>
> Machine-readable decision logs live globally at `~/.agents-devkit/improve/learning/decisions.jsonl` (per-fork, structured). This file is for **human-narrative project decisions that survive across sessions** — the prose that explains *why this codebase looks the way it does* and that adk skills should never silently contradict.

## Decisions

### YYYY-MM-DD — <one-line decision name>

- **Chose:** <option>
- **Why:** <one or two sentences>
- **Rejected:** <option A> — <why>; <option B> — <why>
- **Reversible if:** <condition that would justify revisiting>

(append new decisions at the bottom; never edit old entries — superseding a decision is a new entry that links back to the old one)

